From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: add QSEECOM app start and a TA load probe

Mainline's QSEECOM interface can only look up and talk to apps that
firmware already loaded (uefisecapp on the laptops). Samsung's fingerprint
stack loads its TA from Linux: libbauthtzcommon.so calls
QSEECom_start_app("/vendor/firmware_mnt/image", "securefp", 0x1f4140),
which downstream qseecom turns into the QSEOS APP_START call (owner
QSEE_OS, service APP_MGR, command 1) with the .mdt and every .bNN
segment back to back in one contiguous buffer.

Add qcom_scm_qseecom_app_start() and qcom_scm_qseecom_app_shutdown() for
that, and QCOM_QSEECOM_PROBE, a test module that looks an app up, loads
it from <fw_dir>/<app>.mdt + .bNN through request_firmware() into a TZ
memory pool, and sends it one raw command, in stages set by a module
parameter. The defaults are securefp's BAuth_Type_Check: opcode 0x10 in
a 64-byte request at the start of the shared buffer, the 64-byte reply
at offset 0x40.

INCOMPLETE and listener-blocked results are still not handled; APP_START
reports them as -EIO with the raw result, type and data.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/Kconfig              |  12 +
 drivers/firmware/qcom/Makefile             |   1 +
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_qseecom_probe.c | 266 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c           |  89 ++++++++++
 include/linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h     |  14 ++
 5 files changed, 382 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_qseecom_probe.c

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/Kconfig b/drivers/firmware/qcom/Kconfig
index c7f8413..66b2209 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/Kconfig
@@ -78,6 +78,18 @@ config QCOM_QSEECOM
 
 	  Select Y here to enable the QSEECOM interface driver.
 
+config QCOM_QSEECOM_PROBE
+	tristate "Qualcomm QSEE app load probe"
+	depends on QCOM_QSEECOM
+	help
+	  Test module for bringing up a QSEE trusted application from Linux.
+	  On load it queries the QSEECOM version, looks the app up, and,
+	  depending on the "stage" parameter, loads the app's .mdt/.bNN image
+	  through request_firmware() and sends it one raw command. Everything it
+	  learns goes to the kernel log. It does nothing until it is loaded.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
+
 config QCOM_QSEECOM_UEFISECAPP
 	bool "Qualcomm SEE UEFI Secure App client driver"
 	depends on QCOM_QSEECOM
